  "notes": [
    "Five files: two user-authorized Sony ARWs plus provenance-verified public CC0 Canon CR3/CR2 and Olympus ORF, all outside Git. Anonymous case IDs; no paths, hashes, metadata values or pixels in this artifact.",
    "Fresh process per file/backend/cancellation run. Backends alternate first position. SHA256 checks warm filesystem caches. Single observations, not distributions or cold-media measurements.",
    "LibRaw thumbnail extraction returns compressed bytes without JPEG decode; Photo preview includes orientation/downsampling and decode. Timings have different scope and must not be presented as equivalent ready-to-display measurements.",
    "Photo metadata runs after first preview (shared SDK initialization); LibRaw metadata open is its first API stage. Presence flags are not EXIF value-accuracy or timezone validation.",
    "Optional camera JPEG extraction creates an exclusive private scratch file, measures its write separately and deletes it after the ImageIO test. Extracted JPEG decode/detail timings include scratch filesystem I/O and a fresh process; they are camera-processed JPEG pixels, not RAW detail.",
    "LibRaw full uses camera WB, sRGB 8-bit and otherwise defaults; Apple detail uses existing progressive CIRAWFilter settings. First viewport/full timings, dimensions and RSS do not establish equivalent image quality/color/crop/orientation.",
    "LibRaw cancellation is requested before unpack and checks its progress callback; this does not prove bounded mid-decode cancellation for every camera. Photo cancellation/session regressions are separate.",
    "Peak RSS is per standalone process and includes framework/decoder/transient allocations; neither it nor retained cache bytes is a whole-app memory limit. No runtime LibRaw dependency or backend adoption."
  ]
}
